            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for to infect, then the Spanish for to sneeze."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: quemarse",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "quemarse — \"to burn oneself; to get sunburnt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Me quemé la mano con la sartén. I burned my hand on the frying pan."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Quemarse + body part. Quemarse al sol — to get sunburnt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "quemarse is the reflexive of quemar, which is inherited from Latin cremāre \"to burn\" (EtymDB); English cremate is the same Latin verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
